# Ruling DD (Jimmy, 15 November): `^Display` is text for people, `^Debug` text for
# debugging and for the transcript. A placeholder displays: a text and a character as
# themselves, a number as its digits, a `Bool` as its name. `Debug` quotes a text and
# writes a character as its literal. A generic placeholder bounded by `^Display` displays
# at the type it is given (`Framed`). Expected transcript derived by hand.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

Framed: fn a -> Text where a: ^Display
fn Framed x = "[{x}]"

@page: @unit
@page:
    let word = "hi"
    Ui.Label($text=$"{word} {'q'} {7} {True}")                            # 0
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Debug word} {Debug 'q'} {Debug 7}")                 # 1
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Framed word} {Framed 'q'} {Display 7}")             # 2
